" commit="f523aef38be3a4793b786de53af5d82d4d4d99e7" commit_message="crash: Collect native ARC crashes on x86_64  This CL adds the GYP configuration for building core_collector32, and makes the ARC collector invoke core_collector32 on x86_64.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:*259276 BUG=b:28304295 TEST=cat core | core_collector32  Change-Id: I123f33ad339ab228f4ea25f4fa39ad64d828c552 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/341782 Commit-Ready: Dominik Laskowski &lt;domlaskowski@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Dominik Laskowski &lt;domlaskowski@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="341782" owner_email="domlaskowski@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/82/341782/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7072415a06238c7db96528cfcc13d1e38a9613e2" commit="7f56b7ed86e12605107dc6afe52b6fae42451182" commit_message="Add Service::OnDefaultServiceStateChanged() callback  This allows VPNs to figure out when the default physical service has transitioned back to the Online state, so they can trigger a reconnection.  Bug: None BUG=chromium:598781 TEST=`FEATURES=test emerge-link shill`  (cherry picked from commit e5fb49474296421454309d1995890613a0da9ceb)  Change-Id: I7072415a06238c7db96528cfcc13d1e38a9613e2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/345705 Commit-Ready: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="345705" owner_email="deymo@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" ref="refs/changes/05/345705/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I42d6a90e16e5b3a3834fba6e0e249b0d45226e03" commit="12ab3fa8a9745b393751a416a2c014bbf629e859" commit_message="Initate VPN reconnections when the default physical service is Online  The current logic tries to reconnect the VPN when the default physical service changes, and is in any of the connected states.  This means that it will try to reconnect even if a portal was detected and shill is waiting for the user to authenticate to the portal.  This is not desirable because the device does not have internet access in Portal state.  Change it so that it waits until the default service is Online before attempting a reconnection.  Bug: None BUG=chromium:598781 TEST=`FEATURES=test emerge-link shill`  (cherry picked from commit 8e3ac1b9da21aac8c0e97049e0a0c8326f32e3ba)  Change-Id: I42d6a90e16e5b3a3834fba6e0e249b0d45226e03 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/345706 Commit-Ready: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="345706" owner_email="deymo@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/aosp/platform/system/connectivity/shill" ref="refs/changes/06/345706/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I94d7db893ed3c33c041072c6f42fc6daaa52357d" commit="031b5e72af043480fee353cf2bbb8d973ea5350d" commit_message="Add basic W25Q40EW support  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53035 BRANCH=none TEST=compiled only  Change-Id: I94d7db893ed3c33c041072c6f42fc6daaa52357d Signed-off-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/342817 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="342817" owner_email="dhendrix@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_nu